      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Zahradník et al.",
        "AbstractText": "Strain Pantoea agglomerans JM1 was isolated from the soil of a microbiome that had been exposed to polluting pharmaceuticals. The bacterium exhibited enzymatic activities useful for the biotransformation of beta-lactams. The genome of the strain was assembled and described, and the gene encoding valacyclovir-like hydrolase was identified."
      },
